1. Purpose
This document defines the initial functional and non-functional requirements, business rules, actors, and scope for the FashionHub User Service. It guides detailed design, implementation, testing, and client-facing explanation.
2. Product Context
FashionHub is a clothing-focused e-commerce platform. The User Service owns customer and administrator identity, account lifecycle, authentication, authorization, customer profile, contact verification, and customer address information.
The service does not own product catalog, cart, order, inventory, payment, or shipping data. Those responsibilities belong to their respective services.
3. Goals and Scope
3.1 In scope
•	Customer self-registration.
•	Controlled provisioning of administrator accounts.
•	Login using email OR phone number with password.
•	Email and phone verification workflows.
•	Customer profile and address management.
•	Password change and password reset.
•	Account status and role management.
•	Logout and token/session invalidation strategy.
•	Security-related audit events.
3.2 Out of scope
•	Product browsing and management – Catalog Service.
•	Cart creation and item management – Cart Service.
•	Checkout and order lifecycle – Order Service / checkout workflow.
•	Stock management – Inventory Service.
•	Payment processing and refunds – Payment Service.
•	Shipment and delivery tracking – Shipping Service.
4. Actors
Actor	Description / interactions
Guest	Visitor who is not authenticated; can register and browse public storefront features.
Customer	Registered shopper; can authenticate and manage their own profile and addresses.
Admin	Authorized administrator; can perform permitted administrative operations, including controlled admin provisioning.
Email/SMS Provider	External delivery integration for verification messages. A local/mock adapter will be used during the initial learning build.

