10. Assumptions and Open Design Items
•	The initial implementation is a learning/MVP build and does not claim production certification or compliance.
•	Real email/SMS delivery, hosting, domain, and cloud infrastructure may require a client-approved budget later.
•	Token strategy, expiry, refresh-token storage, and logout semantics will be finalized in Security Design.
•	Administrator provisioning controls, approval/audit requirements, and recovery process will be finalized in detailed design.
•	Profile fields, address fields, password policy, verification expiry, resend limits, and account-lock thresholds will be specified before implementation.
11. Requirements Phase Acceptance Criteria
•	Service boundaries and responsibilities are agreed.
•	Customer and administrator registration policies are documented.
•	Email-or-phone login behavior is documented.
•	The at-least-one-contact verification rule before checkout is documented.
•	Cart and Catalog responsibilities remain outside the User Service boundary.
•	Use case actors and use cases are reviewed before diagram approval.
